Hi, All.

The UG Committee would like to promote our two Geography Day events next Wednesday. A graphic is attached that you can share in your classes and on social media.

The first event is our annual Donut Day tabling from 9–11 a.m. in front of White Hall CB. We'll have free coffee and donuts with an opportunity to meet and greet with students. The second event is our booth at The Curiosity Fair from 4–6 p.m. in the Student Center Ballroom.

Booth events will have geography related activities, including a geocache, map interpretation, and marking your hometown on a map. The Donut Day will conclude with a raffle for maps. If you are free that day, please stop by and say hello.

Finally, if you have any ideas for short, 5-minute activities that could engage passersby, please let us know.

Save the date for April 4, 2024: Cartography in the Bluegrass II

Cartography in the Bluegrass has two goals:

- to bring together current and former students in our mapping program to share their work and experiences, and
- invite the broader community, and specifically potential majors/minors, to learn about the importance of maps and mapping.

We are developing a CFP, but we have a shortlist of former students we would like to invite first. If you have any suggestions for presenters, please let us know.

The event will be held in the Cornerstone Esports theater with a live stream for remote attendees. We'll have an hour of presentations and then a poster session in the lobby where students and participants can share and discuss their work. We working on a some sort of map competition, but haven't worked out the details yet.

If you have any mapping students who would like to present a map, or are teaching a mapping or data viz course next semester, please encourage them to keep this event on their radar.